						<r3d:remarks>TreeBASE is covered by Thomson Reuters Data Citation Index. In previous years the database has been hosted by the Yale Peabody Museum, the San Diego Supercomputer Center, the University at Buffalo, Harvard University, Leiden University, and the University of California, Davis. Development of TreeBASE is hosted at SourceForge. All source code can be downloaded from the TreeBASE subversion repository at SourceForge under a BSD license.
There are no fees for upload, but there are limits to the data size. The interface starts to choke when alignment lengths exceed 200,000 or so.
Wikipedia: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TreeBASE
TreeBASE wiki: https://github.com/TreeBASE</r3d:remarks>
